 >   Anyway. To my point. Can I survive in a puddle if I test the boots or 
 > amulet? 

You can.  If you walk into water there is a chance that you manage
to get out.  I found this when I was trying to get the last
charge out of my wand of cold and typed the direction key too many times.
I even got up on the other side!  (The water was only 1 square of water,
guess what I had used the other charges on...)
There also is a chance to drown.  If you do a risky test, use both
the amulet and the boots in order to maximize chance to survive.

>Do I have to remove all armor etc. ? 

I don't think it would help.  Boots/amulet works well even when you
have other armor.
 > How does the drowning happen
 > in NetHack (obviously, I don't want to find out empirically... :I ) ?
Drowning happens if you get into water without proper equipment, and isn't
lucky enough to get out immediately.
 >   And should I look out for the giant eels? Can they kill you if you wear
 > magical breathing or levitation or water walking?
You should be careful with them, I have read that they may drag you under and
hold you there.  I don't think that would be dangerous with an
amulet, but eels may still kill you by normal fighting.  
 >   Can I kill the Medusa by just putting on my blindcloth and hitting her ?
Yes, all monsters can be killed by hitting.  I tried this, and Medusa
dug a hole down to the castle level.  When I got there, I found that
she was on the other side of the level, so I stupidly
took off my blindfold for a while.  I destroyed the drawbridge, and
started zapping bolts of lightning into the crowd in the castle.
Unfortunately, all the doors between the rooms in the castle were open,
and I saw through the castle and saw Medusa :-(
